\p{Let us turn to another colourful result, the \em{Ham Sandwich Theorem}. Like the Borsuk part of LSB, the origin of this also goes back to the Scottish Café in Lwów (or Lemberg): inspired by Borsuk’s Theorem, Hugo Steinhaus asked whether it was always possible to dissect three solids located anywhere in #{\mathbb{R}^3} by an appropriate plane.}

\transclude{CC29}

